What was taken from MACaQ and what was changed:
  - macaq_mlx/port_convert.py: the D1 pre-scale p = clamp(std(W)^0.75 / rms(x)^0.25, 1e-4, 1e4), rounded to bf16
    (quantize/macaq_balance.py), the 64-wide normalized Sylvester Hadamard weight transform
    (llamacpp/llama.cpp/macaq_math.py) and the choice of linears (llamacpp/prepare_weight_only_gguf.py) are
    re-implemented with MLX for mlx-lm's Qwen3.5 model. The activation statistics are collected with the MLX model
    instead of llama-imatrix. The output is an mlx-lm model with MLX affine quantization, not a GGUF.
  - macaq_mlx/qwen3_5_macaq.py: the run-time input transform of MACaQ's llama.cpp fork (src/llama-graph.cpp,
    build_macaq_pre) is re-implemented as an mlx-lm model type, with a selectable precision (pre_dtype).
  - macaq_mlx/port_gptq.py, macaq_mlx/port_layerwise.py: MACaQ's second step (IQ4_XS codebook quantization with
    vector-codebook refinement) is not ported; GPTQ on the transformed weights replaces it.

